
# =============================================================================
# OSINT PIPELINE - CENTRALIZED API KEYS (FULL VERSION)
# =============================================================================
# Every key from api-keys.yaml (theHarvester) and SpiderFoot.cfg is included.
# Status tags used below:
#   [FREE]        genuinely free, no cost ever
#   [FREE TIER]   free usage tier exists, confirmed limits noted where known
#   [TIERED]      SpiderFoot's own docs call this "Tiered API" (usually means
#                 a free tier exists, but SpiderFoot doesn't publish exact
#                 limits - verify on the provider's site)
#   [PAID ONLY]   no free tier
#   [BLOCKED]     free tier exists but gated behind a work/business email
#   [DEFUNCT]     service no longer operates - key is pointless
#   [NOT FOUND]   module name doesn't appear in SpiderFoot's current docs,
#                 may have been removed in a newer version - verify locally
#
# REMOVED per your instructions: LINKEDIN_COOKIE (Apify actor replaces it),
# and the Google Custom Search / Bing Search keys (sfp_googlesearch,
# sfp_bingsearch, sfp_bingsharedip, and socialprofiles' google/bing keys) -
# both APIs are closed to new signups, and you're using SearXNG instead.
# Google Safe Browsing and Google Maps are DIFFERENT, still-active Google
# APIs, so they're kept below - your call whether to use them.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE CONFIGURATION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [LOCAL] Path to the shared SQLite database used across the pipeline for 
# both raw and reviewed data tiers. 
# Used by: lib/db.py
OSINT_DB_PATH=/home/your_user/.local/share/osint/osint_shared.db

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SHARED - used by BOTH theHarvester AND SpiderFoot
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [FREE TIER] 100 free credits on Censys's new 2025 platform (CenQL query
# language). Used by: theHarvester [censys], SpiderFoot [sfp_censys]
CENSYS_ID=
CENSYS_SECRET=

# [FREE TIER] 50 free queries/month. Used by: theHarvester [fullhunt],
# SpiderFoot [sfp_fullhunt]
FULLHUNT_KEY=

# [FREE TIER] 50 free credits/month. Used by: theHarvester [hunter],
# SpiderFoot [sfp_hunter]. NOTE: distinct from check-if-email-exists (no key)
HUNTER_KEY=

# [FREE TIER] 100 free validation credits every month.
# Used by: email_validation.py (Domain-level catch-all detection)
ZEROBOUNCE_KEY=

# [FREE TIER, very limited] theHarvester/SpiderFoot maintainers describe the
# free account as "very limited." Used by: theHarvester [intelx],
# SpiderFoot [sfp_intelx]
INTELX_KEY=

# [FREE TIER] 25 free result pages + 3,000 free API requests/month - one of
# the more generous ones. Used by: theHarvester [leakix], SpiderFoot [sfp_leakix]
LEAKIX_KEY=

# [FREE TIER, reportedly shrinking] 50 free queries/month per theHarvester's
# docs, but SecurityTrails was acquired by Recorded Future -> Mastercard in
# 2025 and independent trackers report the free tier has been restricted
# since. Verify current limits directly. Used by: theHarvester [securityTrails],
# SpiderFoot [sfp_securitytrails]
SECURITYTRAILS_KEY=

# [TIERED, weak free option] Free key is keyword-only, no filters, ~100
# results capped. One-time $49 lifetime membership unlocks real use.
# Used by: theHarvester [shodan], SpiderFoot [sfp_shodan]
SHODAN_KEY=

# [FREE TIER] 500 free requests/day (Community tier, confirmed still intact
# after Oct 2025 repricing). Used by: theHarvester [virustotal],
# SpiderFoot [sfp_virustotal]
VIRUSTOTAL_KEY=

# [PAID ONLY] Breach-search API requires a paid subscription (~$4.50/10min).
# The free public WEB search (haveibeenpwned.com) still works fine for
# manual one-off lookups - just not via API.
# Used by: theHarvester [haveibeenpwned], SpiderFoot [sfp_haveibeenpwned]
HIBP_KEY=

# [BLOCKED] Free tier exists but requires a work/professional email to
# register (same wall as Hunter.io). SpiderFoot's own docs label this
# "Commercial API" (sfp_projectdiscovery), stronger than "Tiered."
# Used by: theHarvester [projectDiscovery], SpiderFoot [sfp_projectdiscovery]
PROJECTDISCOVERY_KEY=

# [PAID ONLY] $15 minimum, no free tier.
# Used by: theHarvester [dehashed], SpiderFoot [sfp_dehashed]
DEHASHED_KEY=
DEHASHED_USERNAME=

# [PAID ONLY] $587/month minimum, no free tier.
# Used by: theHarvester [onyphe], SpiderFoot [sfp_onyphe]
ONYPHE_KEY=

# [FREE TIER, non-renewing] 50 queries EVER (lifetime cap, not monthly) -
# effectively unusable for ongoing work. Then $2,950/yr.
# Used by: theHarvester [builtwith], SpiderFoot [sfp_builtwith]
BUILTWITH_KEY=


